WEBVTT

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:11.660
The usual morning...

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.150
The usual road...

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.940
The usual me...

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.460
Hey, how's the math stuff?

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.410
Seriously bad.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.160
I still can't get used to this...

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.750
How is everyone having so much fun...?

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.750
Hey, Miki-chan, good morning!

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.250
Um, yes, good morning, Takayashiki-san...

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.210
"Takayashiki-san"? How cold!

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.370
Just call me Aya!

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.370
Um, Aya-chan...

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.250
Yes!

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.040
Come on, let's get to class!

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.620
Right... It's different now, not like before.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.960
Right... It's different now, not like before.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.530
Good morning, Midori-chan!

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.290
"Midori-chan"?!

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:02.960
Good morning, Ono-san...

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.740
Your name is "Ono Midori," right?

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.580
Yes, you got my name right, but...

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.160
Why are you using my
first name all of a sudden?!

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.460
Come on, it'd be too impersonal
if I kept calling you "class rep."

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.500
Right, Miki-chan?

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.790
Um, yeah...

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:19.750
But still... Aren't you being
a bit over-familiar, Takayashiki-san?

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:23.830
Come on, go ahead and
call me "Aya," Midori-chan.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.330
I'm not trying to be modest!

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.910
Hey, um... Ono-san.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:33.790
Thank you for yesterday, for helping me.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:35.830
As her teammate!

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.370
Oh, don't mention it, that was nothing.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:44.620
No, if I had to do it alone,
I wouldn't have known what to do at all...

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:49.660
But thanks to you, Ono-san, I had a lot of fun.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.870
Takekasa-san...

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:55.250
Well... Don't be so formal.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:59.290
Just call me "Midori."
I'll go ahead and call you "Miki," too.

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:04.290
Don't worry. We're companions
that fought on the same team, right?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.210
Um...

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:06.160
Right?

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.910
Oh... Okay. So then, um...

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:12.410
Midori-chan...

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:17.870
That's good... real good.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.160
Huh?

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.000
What? What, what?

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.940
What is this difference in treatment?

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:03.790
Which seat?
Oh, window seat! Cool.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:06.940
Oh, here's my seat!

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:10.790
I'm Takayashiki Aya.
Nice to meet you, neighbor!

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.280
Yes, same to you.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.820
Nice to meet you, too, other neighbor!

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.580
Oh, yeah, sure, nice to meet ya...

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:26.540
But after that,
I've hardly talked to her at all...

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:29.160
I'm wasting the fact that
I'm sitting next to her...

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:33.300
This needs to change,
I'll do anything to get closer to her!

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.430
I'm so looking forward
to playing after school!

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:39.350
So in this case, you want to
focus on a specific character...

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:39.350
Monomial expression

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:39.350
Polynomial expression

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.040
Looking at the order and coefficient...

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:41.980
Now's my chance!

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:46.460
Huh? Oh...

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.290
Here.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.290
Oh.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:52.370
Thanks...

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.210
Oh, no, I forgot my dictionary!

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:56.710
Hey, you can use mine...

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.330
We can share mine!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.790
Thanks!

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:06.620
Yay! Now all we have left to do is clean!

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:09.160
Looking forward to the game, aren't you?

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.750
This time I won't fail...

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:14.660
Oh, good timing.
Takayashiki-san, here's the dustpan.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.500
Hey, thanks!

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:21.620
Okay, let's go home.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:22.960
Wanna stop somewhere?

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.210
I wouldn't mind getting something sweet.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:27.790
I couldn't talk to her at all...

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:32.660
Why...? How? I had so many opportunities...

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:36.500
Oh, well... Try again tomorrow.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:39.000
The manager looked really scary, didn't he?

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.950
Takayashiki! And... Takekasa?

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.950
The manager looked really scary, didn't he?

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.870
But he was really nice.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:45.500
What are they doing alone?

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.790
I know, right? By the way, did you see
that new café near the station?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.790
Concentrate! It's another chance!

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:49.710
What are you doing?

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:51.210
Oh... Ono.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.040
Oh, it's you, Tanoue.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.750
What is it? If you're not going
inside, get out of my way.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:56.710
Huh?!

00:06:56.710 --> 00:07:00.660
No, I mean, I am going in.
I forgot something...

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:04.000
Oh, there she is! Midori-chan! And...

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.290
You are...?

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:07.410
Oh... Hey.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:10.710
He was the guy that
was staring earlier today...

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:15.750
Oh, you're my neighbor!
Do you two know each other?

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:17.410
Don't pay attention to this guy.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:18.410
What?!

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.620
I've just been stuck in the same classes
as him since pre-school for some reason.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.870
Oh! A childhood friend!

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.580
More like an unfortunate entanglement.

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:27.660
Oh?

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:31.750
Oh, yes! She's so cute!

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:35.160
Tanoue-kun... Could he be...?

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:38.080
What are you doing, all spaced out like that?

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:41.660
You forgot something, right?
Just grab it and go home already.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:43.750
Dammit, Ono...!

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:48.540
How insensitive of her,
she's ruining my chance!

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:53.910
What? Going home already? You should
stick around and play games with us!

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:56.120
Wait, why Tanoue, too?!

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:59.870
Why not? I'm sure these things
are more fun with more people.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:02.960
Hey, do you play games and stuff?

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.870
Y-Yes! I love games!

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.370
Huh? You've literally never said that before.

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:12.250
None of your business! I'm in!

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:14.080
What's up with this guy...?

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.500
Yay!

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:21.930
{Between}

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:26.330
So... what was your name again?

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:29.770
I... I'm Tanoue Shouta.

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:35.460
Yes! Tanoue-kun! I guess we've
never talked, despite being neighbors!

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:38.120
I'm Takayashiki Aya. Good luck!

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.540
Y-You, too!

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.330
And you're sitting across from Miki-chan!

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.040
Hi... Have fun.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.960
Y-Yeah! Same.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:51.500
And of course, you know Midori-chan,
since you're childhood friends, right?

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:53.330
Is it possible to be so lucky?!

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:58.620
Not only is she super cute,
she's super nice as well!

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:01.710
So, Midori-chan, what game
are we playing today?

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.460
Yes, one second.

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.120
Wow!

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.410
What the...? What is this?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:11.910
These are all games...?

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:14.790
Yes. They're all card games.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.960
I've never seen this before...

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.040
So many types!

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:20.210
Yes...

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:23.790
When you say "card games" in Japan,
people think of the regular poker deck or <i>Uno</i>,

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:30.080
and trading card games featuring anime
and video game characters are popular now.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.290
In Europe though, especially around Germany,

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:36.330
people are still making lots
of new games and they're quite popular.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:43.870
The genre is varied, too, like games based
on intellect, or those based on raw luck.

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:47.830
How does she know all this stuff?

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:51.460
I guess she's always been this way,
but I never understand what she's thinking.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:57.320
So for today... let's try this one.
<i>Kaker Laken Poker</i>.

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:00.540
<i>Kaker Laken Poker.</i>..?

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:02.580
What's a "<i>kaker laken</i>"...?

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.540
It's German for "cockroach."

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:09.290
This game features cards depicting
other pests too, for a total of eight.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:15.460
Flies, scorpions, spiders, frogs, and so on.

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:19.330
<i>Cockroach Poker</i> is a bluffing game,

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:22.080
where you force these
pest cards on other players.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.620
A bluffing game?

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:24.870
What's that?

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:28.620
To put it simply,
a game about lying and trickery.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:31.000
L-Lying...

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.000
And trickery...

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:36.160
Here are the rules.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:40.540
The first player hands
another player a card facedown.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:44.370
They say the name of
the pest illustrated on that card.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.710
This is a cockroach!

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:52.250
You can be honest, or you can lie
and say a different pest's name.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:59.620
The receiver of the card guesses if
that was a lie or not, and flips the card.

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:02.160
This is not a cockroach!

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:08.250
If they get it right, the card
is returned to the sender faceup.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:12.660
If they get it wrong, the card is
placed faceup in front of the receiver.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:17.830
The next turn begins with the person
who received the card playing first.

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:19.790
This is a frog!

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:23.790
When someone hands you a card,
you can decide to pass.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.870
When passing...

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.870
This is a bat.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:28.830
I pass.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:32.870
...you declare the pass, then look
at the card without showing others.

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:38.370
You then declare a name of a pest
and hand the card to someone else.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.210
This is a spider!

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:45.290
You can say the same name as the pest
mentioned previously, or change it.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:50.290
If you end up with four of the same
pest cards faceup in front of you,

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:53.830
or if you collect at least one of each
of the eight pest types, you lose.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:56.910
See? Simple, right?

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:58.330
Um, yeah...

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:02.120
I guess I kind of understand...? Or not?

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:04.620
Yes.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:08.460
You'll get it once you try it. Let's start.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:18.830
Okay. You start, Tanoue.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:20.290
G-Got it!

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:21.500
This is my golden opportunity.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:25.910
I'm going to get close
to Takayashiki through this game!

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:28.120
Well then, I'll start with Takayashiki...

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.410
Bring it on!

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:33.540
This is a cockroach.

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:38.290
Um, I'm supposed to guess if this
is a cockroach or not, right?

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:43.370
Yes. If you think it's a cockroach,
say "This is a cockroach" and flip the card.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:49.290
If you think it's another pest,
say "this is not" and flip it.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:53.750
Hmm... But I have no way of telling...

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.080
I'll just guess then.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.500
This is not a cockroach!

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.540
A cockroach...!

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:04.330
N-Not bad, Tanoue-kun!

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:10.660
Oh, no! Terrible first impression!
What am I doing from the get-go!

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:14.960
Since you guessed wrong,
you keep the card faceup.

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:16.580
Okay...

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:20.160
The next turn starts with
whoever failed, so it's you, Aya.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:21.370
Okay!

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:22.830
Returning the favor!

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:25.250
Tanoue-kun! This is a fly!

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:28.580
Oh... hmm... Let's see...

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:33.210
Come on, make your move. A fly, or not a fly?

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:38.750
I have no clue...
but she doesn't seem to be lying.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.710
Well... then yes, it's a fly.

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:44.750
What?! How did you know?!

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.160
Err... Just guessing!

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:52.500
I mean... I can't imagine
Takayashiki lying to anyone...

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:54.370
A second card...

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:57.750
You failed again, so, Aya, play another card.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:13:59.120
Then one more time!

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:01.410
Tanoue-kun! This is a scorpion!

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:07.790
Oh, no... I think this is a scorpion,
but if I keep beating her, I'll look bad...

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.910
What should I do...?

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:15.620
Tanoue-kun really must
be interested in Aya-chan...

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:17.620
This morning, too, he was...

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:24.660
I have no idea, so I guess I'll pass...

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:25.830
Yay!

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:29.160
A scorpion... as I thought.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:31.580
Okay, Takekasa!

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:34.870
This is... um... a fly!

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:39.580
Wh-What...?

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:42.120
Not a fly.

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:45.730
Wow! Miki-chan, you, too?
How are you doing that?

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:50.160
It just felt to me like he was lying...

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.120
Huh...?

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.120
Idiot.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:56.660
If you hesitate before declaring your card,
it's super obvious that you're lying.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:59.410
This girl, she's such a...

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:02.120
Okay then, Ono! This is a stink bug!

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:05.000
It is a stink bug.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.290
What?!

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:11.870
This is your first time playing this game--
the first time you've heard the rules.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:14.080
You should have trouble
memorizing all of the pest types.

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:18.000
"Stink bug" is not a word you can whip
out of nowhere so quickly at that state.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:21.580
If you were lying, you would have
said a word you're more familiar with,

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:24.040
like "cockroach" or "fly."

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:28.580
Oh, no... She knows this game inside out!

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:32.040
Get it? Now play your next card already.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:35.750
Well... To Takekasa, this is a frog.

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:39.330
I pass. Aya-chan, this is a frog.

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:40.870
This is not a frog!

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:43.410
Oh, no! Foiled again!

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:44.620
This is a rat.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.210
I pass.

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:47.960
This is a rat.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:48.870
It is a rat.

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:51.040
Oh, no! Caught again!

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:52.790
This is a stink bug!

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:53.790
It is a stink bug.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:56.080
What...? How?!

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.210
A fly!

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:58.330
It is a fly.

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:00.120
Oh...

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:03.080
Miki-chan! This is a cockroach!

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.290
This is a cockroach.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:07.830
What?! How?!

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:11.000
Impressive, Miki.
You're right almost every time.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:15.160
Yeah... I think this game suits me.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:18.330
Oh, no! I've failed again!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.830
This is bad...

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:23.870
Takayashiki now has
three cockroaches and flies.

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:28.160
Get either one and she loses the game...

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:31.620
She's not capable of deceiving others.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:33.160
She's an angel...

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:36.460
Here, it's your turn, Aya.

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:37.910
Yeah...

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:41.460
I have to try to make sure
Takayashiki doesn't lose...

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:45.250
Okay, Tanoue-kun! This is a cockroach!

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:47.750
Cockroach?!

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:53.040
If I say "yes" and push
the card back to her, she'll lose!

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.080
Who would play such a risky card?!

00:16:55.080 --> 00:17:00.960
Ah, I get it, she's lying.
This must not be a cockroach.

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:04.330
She really is a very bad liar.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:09.460
But if I call her out on it and push
the card back, that would be mean, too...

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:12.790
I should just pass and play Mr. Nice Guy...

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:17.870
Wait a second, I've also got
three bats. I'm on the verge, too!

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:20.830
If this card is a bat...

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:25.790
Actually, that's likely,
since she's attacking me!

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:29.160
I could pass and do a showdown with Ono...

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:31.790
No! There's no way I can beat her!

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:36.160
That said, Takekasa has
a near-perfect score as well...

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:41.500
Tanoue-kun must be trying
hard to save Aya-chan...

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:44.910
She must have a really sharp intuition.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:48.540
She's probably really good
at gauging other people's emotions...

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:51.750
What should I do?!
If I pass, to protect Takayashiki,

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:54.830
I could get smashed by one
of the other two and lose the game.

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:57.000
I don't want to lose!

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.580
Tanoue!

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:01.620
What'll it be? A showdown, or a pass?

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:03.620
Just... wait a sec, okay?

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:09.330
If you think about it, if this is a bat,
I could send it back to Takayashiki,

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:13.330
and it wouldn't make her lose the game,
because she doesn't have any bats.

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:14.790
In that case...!

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:15.620
Showdown!

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:16.580
What?!

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:19.620
This is not a cockroach!

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:23.750
What the...? Huh!? A fly?!

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:27.290
So you now have four flies, and...

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:30.410
Oh, no! I lost!

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:34.410
That was dumb. You can't play the card
that would lose you the game.

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:40.370
I thought he'd pass! I wanted
to get rid of the risky card!

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:43.710
Boo! Tanoue-kun, you idiot!

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:50.330
I've been trying hard to pass,
but at the very end...

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:53.980
Total backfire! I gave the finishing blow!

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:58.270
Why are you depressed, too...?

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:03.660
Oh... Tanoue-kun,
he was trying so hard for Aya-chan...

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.460
Well... I guess I'll be leaving now.

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:09.040
Oh, hey, wait!

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.500
Huh...?

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.160
Do you have a moment?

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:25.710
Wh-What is it, Takayashiki...?

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:29.660
Um, sorry if I'm wrong, but...

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:35.370
Before we played, when you
said you forgot something...

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:36.870
...that was a lie, right?

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:40.290
Huh? Um... Uh...

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:42.290
Why would you think...?

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:44.620
So what did you forget then?!

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.830
That's... uh...

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:53.330
It's okay. I've figured it out.

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.750
You've figured it out...?

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:58.710
Don't hide it. I might not be good at games,

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:02.710
but my female intuition is
really sharp with these things.

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:07.580
What?! Did she figure it out? That I like her?

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:11.330
Wait, does she, too?

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:13.370
Does she like me back...?!

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:16.120
So... Tanoue-kun, you...

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:19.410
...have a thing for Midori-chan, right?

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:21.660
Huh? Midori-chan?

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:26.080
Wait, what?! Ono?! No, no, no, impossible!

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:28.120
Me, Ono?! Why?!

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:31.540
Don't be shy!
Childhood friends, right? Awesome!

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:34.160
I knew there was something going on.
If it didn't include someone you liked,

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:36.620
why would you jump into a group
with three girls to play a game?

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:40.660
Well, that's, uh... um... It's...

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:44.080
What's taking Aya so long? What is she doing?

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:48.660
I think Midori-chan is great.
She's a bit weird, but she's super pretty.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:52.750
She does seem like she has her guard up,
but I can help you with that!

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:53.710
Seriously, I mean, it's not--

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:55.250
Don't worry about it!

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:55.250
Seriously, I mean, it's not--

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.960
Feel free to talk to me about it, okay?

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:58.160
See you tomorrow! Bye!

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.250
Oh... Hey, wait...!

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:02.790
Let's play again! <i>Cockroach Poker</i>!

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:05.620
Seriously, Takayashiki...?

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:08.750
Your "female intuition" is way off, too...!

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:15.000
Wow, today was super
fun, too! Right, Miki-chan?

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.330
Yes.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:17.540
By the way...

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:21.960
Tanoue-kun likes Midori-chan.
Did you notice?

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:23.000
Huh...?

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:25.500
Oh, Midori-chan, what a girl, am I right?

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:27.330
What? Did you say something?

00:21:27.330 --> 00:21:29.040
Nope, nothing.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:33.910
Hey, Midori-chan, let's play games again.
We can invite Tanoue-kun, too!

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:35.710
Huh? Why him?!

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:39.710
Come on, the more the merrier, right?

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:41.410
I guess...

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:47.960
...hanging out with classmates before going
home was unimaginable to me before.

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:52.960
This is fun...

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:54.280
Miki-chan!

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:56.830
Hurry! We're leaving without you!

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:58.240
Oh, wait!

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:04.210
I hope the way home is always this fun...

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:39.960
We're all playing games at my house!

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:43.660
My sister's friend, Maki-chan, joins the fray!

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:46.390
Huh? Where have you seen Miki-chan before?
